From 3643c2da7a4fc091b4def469b1eb5044f5350311 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:13:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(schema): five invented prices out of the JSON-LD, and the
 old domain consolidated
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

root-schema.ts was handing Google five project price ranges — $4,000-$15,000 and
four more — that appear nowhere else on this site, derive from nothing, and that
nobody could check including us. It also repeated the ~99.7% dust figure already
recorded as unsourced in CLAIMS_REGISTER.

Twenty-five guards were watching the pages and none was watching the schema.
That is the wrong way round: an unsourced number on a page is read by a human
who can weigh it in context, the same number in JSON-LD is quoted by a machine
as fact to someone who never visits. The most consequential place to be wrong
was the least guarded place.

servicePriceRange() now reads the same published band the service page renders
and returns undefined where none is published. A project total needs an area
assumption this site does not publish, so it is not published here either. The
dust sentence describes the mechanism instead of a number.

verify-schema-figures.mjs is the twenty-sixth guard: no currency amount and no
percentage as a literal anywhere under lib/schema or lib/graph. Interpolations
pass. Comments stripped first, because flagging this repo's own explanation of
why it does not publish a number is F-58/F-106/F-163/F-175 for a fifth time.
Proven by injecting both figure types.

Also: four permanent path-preserving redirects from ecowoodshardwood.com to
ecowoods.ca. 301 not 302, because a temporary redirect tells a crawler to keep
the old URL indexed. Path-preserving not all-to-homepage, because a link to
/services/floor-refinishing should land on floor refinishing. The precondition —
adding the domain to this Vercel project — cannot be done from the repository,
so until then the rules match nothing and are inert.

F-197 records a conditional I cannot resolve and will not guess at: .hero-bg
declares no url(), RotatingBackground returns null on an empty pool, and
/api/backgrounds returns an empty pool without UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY. If that
variable is unset in Vercel the homepage hero has no photograph. Five-second
check, owner's to make.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
